    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a framework compile-time constant. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>has_value</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a framework expression type (see <computeroutput>extension::is_op</computeroutput>) with a static <computeroutput>value</computeroutput> member, like <computeroutput>integral_constant</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>floating_point_constant</computeroutput>, the types of the numeric literals. The comparators compare such operands by their <computeroutput>T::value</computeroutput> constants.</para>
<para>The types of the application are excluded, even if they have a member named <computeroutput>value</computeroutput>, so that they are compared with their own operators. </para>
